\ Interpreter-free coverage for a quotation literal swapped under a value. `swap` relabels its two
\ entries without moving them, so the quotation can sit at an index whose physical slot still holds
\ the value another entry reads. Building the quotation must not overwrite that slot. Output must
\ match the interpreter.
quotation-under-swap: ( a b -- b q ) [ swap [ 7 8 + ] swap drop ] ;

1 2 quotation-under-swap
call .
.

\ The original report: a task handle swapped above a channel, then a quotation sent through it.
[
  <channel> dup
  [ receive call ] curry spawn
  swap [ 7 8 + ] swap send
  await .
] task-scope
